# Git — MCP commit only

- **Forbidden:** `git commit`, `git push`, `git rebase`/`cherry-pick` that create commits, `clean_commit.py`, `gh pr create`, `gh release create`.
- **Allowed:** `git merge` (owner decision, 2026-09-13), run with no `-C`/`--git-dir` override so it only ever touches your own current worktree — it never rewrites history and can only fold a sibling branch's already-committed work into the current branch, never touching the branch merged from. A conflicted merge stops with no commit; finishing it still needs a real `git commit`/`git merge --continue`, which stays forbidden — hand a conflict back to the owner rather than resolving and committing it yourself.
- **Allowed commit path:** MCP `repo-git.commit` (and optional `repo-git.validate_message`) — commit as part of finishing a task without waiting to be asked.
- **Commit often:** one logical change per commit, at each verified increment and task boundary — not once at the end of the session. Pass explicit `paths`; leave other streams' dirty files alone. A correction is a new commit, never an amend.
- **Verify first:** run the subsystem's test/lint/guard, or say in the body that it could not run.
- **Push:** owner only. Never push from the agent.
- No `Co-authored-by`, no vendor/AI watermark trailers.
- See `docs/contributing/agent-git.md`.
